hadiths[33]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1070","It is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Whoever frees his share in a jointly owned slave, and he has enough wealth equal to the value of the slave, then the slave's value should be assessed justly. All the partners should be given the price of their shares (from his wealth), and the slave should be freed on his behalf. Otherwise, whatever portion of the slave has been freed, is freed."""
"1071","It is narrated from Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If a slave is jointly owned between two partners, and one of them frees his share, if the one who frees is wealthy, then the highest or fair price will be set, which is neither less nor more, and then the share will be taken from him with wealth."""
"1072","Saeed bin Musayyib (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates that a woman or a man freed his six slaves, while he had no other wealth besides them. This matter was brought before the Prophet ﷺ, so he ﷺ drew lots among the slaves and freed one third of them (i.e., two). Imam Shafi’i (may Allah have mercy on him) said: This incident of freeing (the slaves) was during the illness in which the person died."
"1073","It is narrated from Imran bin Husain (may Allah be pleased with him) that a man from among the Ansar made a bequest at the time of his death and freed six slaves, and he had no wealth other than them. Or he said (the narrator is unsure whether the words were): At the time of his death, he freed six slaves and had nothing besides them. This matter reached the Prophet ﷺ, and he ﷺ expressed strong displeasure at this. Then he ﷺ called for those slaves, divided them into three groups, and by drawing lots, freed two of them, and kept four as slaves (in the ownership of the heirs)."
"1074","Narrated from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: Barirah (may Allah be pleased with her) came to me and said: ""I have entered into a contract of manumission with my masters for nine uqiyah of silver, to be paid in installments of one uqiyah per year, so please help me."" Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said to her: ""If your masters wish that I pay them this amount, I am ready to do so, but your freedom will be attributed to me."" Barirah (may Allah be pleased with her) went to her masters and told them this, but they refused. She returned from her masters while the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was present, and she said: ""I presented this to them but they refused to accept it unless the wala’ (right of inheritance/loyalty) would be for them."" When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) heard this, he asked her about the whole matter, and Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) informed him. Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to her: ""Buy her and stipulate the condition of wala’ for them, for wala’ is only for the one who sets free."" So Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) did so. Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) stood among the people, praised and glorified Allah, and then said: ""What is the matter with some people who stipulate conditions that are not in the Book of Allah? Any condition that is not in the Book of Allah is invalid, even if there are a hundred such conditions. The decision of Allah is truer and His condition is stronger, and indeed, wala’ is for the one who sets free."""
"1075","It is narrated in a similar manner through another chain from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her)."
"1076","Narrated Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her): The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Indeed, the right of wala' belongs to the one who sets free."""
"1077","It is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that he reported from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that she bought a slave girl with the intention of freeing her. Her owners said: ""We sell her to you on the condition that her wala’ (right of inheritance/loyalty) will be for us."" She mentioned this to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), and he said: ""Do not let this prevent you (from freeing her), for wala’ belongs to the one who sets free."""
"1078","Yahya bin Saeed narrated from Umrah, as a mursal narration, without mentioning (Sayyidah) Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her)."
"1079","Narrated from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: Barirah (may Allah be pleased with her) came to me and said: ""I have made a contract of emancipation with my masters for nine uqiyahs of silver, paying one uqiyah each year, so please help me."" Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said to her: ""If your masters wish, I am ready to give them this money, but your wala (allegiance) will be for me."" Barirah (may Allah be pleased with her) went to her masters (and then returned) while the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was present. She came and said: ""I presented this matter to them, but they refused unless the wala remains with them."" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) heard this and asked her about it, so Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) told him the whole story. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Buy her and stipulate the condition of wala, for wala is for the one who sets free."" So Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) did so. Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) stood among the people, praised Allah, and said: ""What is the matter with some people who stipulate conditions which are not in Allah's Book? Any condition that is not in Allah's Book is invalid, even if there are a hundred such conditions. Allah's decision is truer and His condition is firmer, and indeed, wala is for the one who sets free."""
"1080","It is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that she intended to buy a slave girl in order to set her free. The owner said: ""We sell her to you on the condition that her wala' (right of inheritance/loyalty) will be attributed to us."" When Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) mentioned this to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""Do not let this prevent you (from setting her free), and indeed, wala' belongs to the one who sets free."""
"1081","It is narrated from ‘Amrah bint ‘Abd al-Rahman that Barirah (may Allah be pleased with her) came seeking help, so ‘A’ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: “If your masters are pleased that I pay your price to them in one lump sum and set you free, I will do so.” Barirah (may Allah be pleased with her) conveyed this to her masters, but they said: “No, except that your wala’ (allegiance) will be for us.” Imam Malik (may Allah have mercy on him) said that Yahya said: ‘Amrah thinks that ‘A’ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) mentioned this to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), so he (ﷺ) said: “Do not let this (condition) prevent you (from freeing her). Buy her and set her free, for the wala’ is for the one who sets free.”"
"1082","A man from Banu Sulaym narrates from Sinin bin Abi Jameelah that during the time of Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him), he found a child lying on the road, so he brought the child to Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him). He (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""What made you pick up this soul?"" He replied: ""It was being lost, so I picked it up."" My master said to him: ""O Commander of the Faithful! He is a righteous man."" Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""Is that so?"" He replied: ""Yes."" Then Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""You may go, this child is free, his wala' (allegiance) is for you, and his expenses are our responsibility."""
"1083","Abu Bakr bin Abdur Rahman bin Harith bin Hisham narrated that As bin Hisham died and he left behind three sons: two full brothers and one half-brother (from a different mother). One of the full brothers died and left behind wealth and freed slaves as inheritance. His full brother became the heir of his wealth and the wala’ (right of allegiance) of his freed slaves. Then the one who inherited the wealth and the wala’ of the slaves also died, and among his heirs were a son and a half-brother. So his son said: “I am the heir of the wealth and the wala’ of the freed slaves which my father had acquired.” But the deceased’s brother said: “The matter is not like that, because you have inherited the wealth, but not the wala’ of the slaves. What do you think—if my brother had died today, would I not have been his heir?” So both of them brought their dispute to Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him), and he decided the wala’ of the freed slaves in favor of the brother."
"1084","It is narrated from Ata bin Abi Rabah that Tariq bin Murraq set his household slaves free as Saibah, then his inheritance came. So Umar bin Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, said: ""Give this to the heirs of Tariq,"" but they refused to take it, so Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: ""Distribute it among people like them."""
"1085","It is narrated from Ata that Tariq bin Marqa’ freed some slaves as Saibah among his family in Yemen. Then he left ten thousand and some inheritance. When this matter was mentioned to Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him), he ordered me to return this to Tariq or to the heirs of Tariq. I have some doubt about this matter in the narration."
"1086","It is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Prophet (ﷺ) forbade selling or gifting of wala'."
"1087","It is narrated from Mujahid that Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""Wala' is like a contract (agreement); I will maintain it exactly where Allah the Exalted has placed it."""
"1088","It is narrated from Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) forbade selling or gifting of wala'."
"1089","It is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade the selling and gifting of wala'."
"1090","It is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""Wala' is a bond just like the bond of lineage; it should neither be sold nor gifted."""
"1091","Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that Abu Mazkoor was a man from the tribe of Uzrah. He had a Coptic slave whom he had declared as Mudabbar. The Prophet ﷺ heard about this slave, so he ﷺ sold the slave and said: ""When any of you is poor, he should begin with himself; if there is surplus wealth, then he should start with those under his care, and then if he finds surplus wealth after that, he should give charity to others."""
"1092","It is narrated from Amr bin Dinar that a man, after his death, instructed for the emancipation of his slave, while he had no other wealth besides him. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Who will buy him from me?"" Na’eem bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) bought him for eight hundred dirhams and paid its price."
"1093","From another chain, it is narrated from Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both) from the Prophet ﷺ similar to the previous hadith."
"1094","It is narrated from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: A man from the tribe of Banu Udhrah made his slave a Mudabbar (a slave who is set free after the master's death). When the Prophet (ﷺ) was informed, he asked: ""Do you have any wealth besides him?"" He replied: ""No."" Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Who will buy this slave from me?"" Na’eem bin Abdullah Al-Adawi (may Allah be pleased with him) bought him from the Prophet (ﷺ) for eight hundred dirhams. He brought the amount to the Prophet (ﷺ), and the Prophet (ﷺ) handed over the price to the owner. Then he said: ""Start with yourself and spend on it. If anything is left from yourself, then on your family. If anything is left from your family, then on your relatives. If anything is still left, then here and there, to the right and left (i.e., to other deserving people), spend it."""
"1095","Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates: One of us made his slave a Mudabbar, and he had no other wealth except that slave. The Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""Who will buy this slave from me?"" Nu'aim bin Nahham (may Allah be pleased with him) bought him. Amr said: I heard Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) say that he was a Coptic slave and he died in the first year of the caliphate of Abdullah bin Zubair (may Allah be pleased with them both). Abu Zubair added these words: His name was Yaqub."
"1096","Imam Shafi’i, may Allah have mercy on him, said: I generally heard it from them in this way during my time, then I found in my book that “one of us made a slave a mudabbar and he died.” This (phrase) is either a mistake in my book or a mistake from Sufyan, may Allah have mercy on him. If this mistake is from Sufyan, then Ibn Jurayj and Abu’l-Zubayr are more reliable in remembering the hadith than Sufyan, and then with Ibn Jurayj, Layth and others also narrate this (Ibn Jurayj’s) hadith. And Abu’l-Zubayr also mentions the limit of the mudabbar’s life in the hadith. And Hammad ibn Zayd, Hammad ibn Salamah, and others besides them are more reliable in remembering the hadith of ‘Amr than Sufyan alone. The reliability in memorizing hadith is established because of the mistakes I found in the hadith of Ibn Jurayj and Layth from Abu’l-Zubayr. And in the hadith of Hammad, which is from ‘Amr, and others besides Hammad who narrate from ‘Amr, they narrate it just as Hammad ibn Zayd narrated it. And among those who met Sufyan ibn ‘Uyaynah earlier than me, several told me that he did not mention the word “died” (māt) in his hadith. And when I told them that I found the word “died” in my book, some of them were surprised. Imam Shafi’i, may Allah have mercy on him, said: Perhaps this is a mistake or slip that I remembered from them."
"1097","It is narrated from Umrah that Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) had a slave girl whom she had made a mudabbir. This slave girl performed magic on her, and then she also confessed to the magic. So Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) ordered regarding her that she should be sold to those villagers who treat their slaves badly, and thus she was sold."
"1098","It is narrated from Mujahid that Zaid bin Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him) said regarding a mukatab slave: ""As long as even one dirham (of payment) remains upon him, he is still a slave."""
"1099","It is narrated from Ismail bin Umayyah that Nafi’ informed him that Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) made a contract of manumission (mukataba) with his slave for thirty thousand. Then that slave came to him and said, “I am unable (to pay the amount).” Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) said, “Then erase your contract of manumission.” He said, “I am helpless, you erase it yourself.” Nafi’ said, “I signaled to that slave to erase it because (Ibn Umar) wanted to set him free.” That slave erased the contract; he had one or two sons. Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) said, “Separate from my slave-girl.” Nafi’ said: Later, Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) also set his son free."
"1100","It is narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is the right of the slave to have food and clothing in a good manner from his master, and he should only be assigned work according to his capacity."""
"1101","It is narrated from Utbah bin Abi Lahab that he heard Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) say regarding slaves: ""Feed them what you eat yourself, and clothe them with what you wear yourself."""
"1102","It is narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the servant of any one of you protects him from the heat and smoke of cooking, then at the time of eating, he should make him sit with him. If this is not possible, then he should give him a tasty morsel from that food, or grant it to him."" Or he said a word of similar meaning (the narrator is in doubt)."
